WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.991 --> 00:00:15.992
For three days Jo and the girls kept their distance from the boys.

2
00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:24.454
Nan took delight in ignoring them, but Daisy didn't like being separated from her twin.

3
00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:30.156
At last the boys couldn't take it anymore and appealed to Mr.

4
00:00:30.236 --> 00:00:31.116
Bauer for help.

5
00:00:33.304 --> 00:00:38.025
"To win the girls back, you must do something nice for them," the professor advised.

6
00:00:40.326 --> 00:00:46.207
So Tommy, Nat, and Demi retreated to the attic, where they embarked on a secret project.

7
00:00:49.928 --> 00:00:53.109
Asia grumbled about the amount of paste they were using.

8
00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:01.171
Nan was so curious that she almost got her nose pinched in the attic door while spying.

9
00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:06.951
Meanwhile Daisy lamented that they couldn't all play nicely together.

10
00:01:08.813 --> 00:01:12.696
When the boys were finally ready, Demi marched into Jo's study.

11
00:01:12.716 --> 00:01:18.521
"Please, Aunt Jo, will you and the girls come outside for a party?"

12
00:01:18.941 --> 00:01:19.582
he asked.

13
00:01:19.602 --> 00:01:22.965
"Are you sure I won't be in the way?"

14
00:01:23.465 --> 00:01:24.206
Jo asked.

15
00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:25.847
"Oh, no!"

16
00:01:26.247 --> 00:01:27.348
Demi reassured her.

17
00:01:27.368 --> 00:01:31.312
"The party will be spoiled if you're not there."

18
00:01:34.364 --> 00:01:39.926
Soon Nan, Daisy, and Bess were packed into a wagon drawn by Toby the donkey.

19
00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.648
Jo followed behind with Rob and Teddy.

20
00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:51.011
When they came to a hill, they stopped, but there was no sign of a party.

21
00:01:54.252 --> 00:01:56.913
Nan climbed out of the wagon, looking annoyed.

22
00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:59.094
"What's the point of this?"

23
00:01:59.514 --> 00:02:00.235
she demanded.

24
00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:02.335
"Hush, Nan!"

25
00:02:02.756 --> 00:02:06.238
Jo said, wanting the boys' peace effort to succeed.

26
00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:10.501
But luckily Demi was not discouraged at all.

27
00:02:10.521 --> 00:02:17.706
"If you stand right here," he promised, "a surprise will come to you."

28
00:02:20.848 --> 00:02:25.712
He disappeared behind a large rock, and the girls heard some minor arguing.

29
00:02:25.732 --> 00:02:31.476
"No, you take that one because I'm taking this one," Demi said.

30
00:02:32.756 --> 00:02:37.740
Just when the girls couldn't bear the suspense another moment, the boys appeared.

31
00:02:39.121 --> 00:02:44.646
Each was carrying a new kite, which they presented to Daisy, Nan, and Bess.

32
00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:51.652
The girls shrieked with delight, but Demi silenced them.

33
00:02:51.672 --> 00:02:57.456
"This isn't the whole surprise," he said with a face full of merriment.

34
00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:05.114
The boys disappeared behind the rock and reappeared bearing a giant kite this time.

35
00:03:06.576 --> 00:03:08.637
On it was printed "For Mrs.

36
00:03:08.757 --> 00:03:11.159
Bauer" in bright yellow letters.

37
00:03:11.179 --> 00:03:18.104
"We made this for you because you were angry with us and took the girls' side," Nat explained.

38
00:03:18.124 --> 00:03:21.406
"So we owe you an apology too."

39
00:03:26.464 --> 00:03:32.186
All the boys began to shake with laughter because Jo looked so surprised by their gift.

40
00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:39.209
She clapped her hands and joined in the laughter, delighted with their thoughtfulness.

41
00:03:39.229 --> 00:03:46.932
"When we told Uncle Fritz about our plan, he said you'd like a kite too," Demi said.

42
00:03:46.952 --> 00:03:52.094
"He always knows what I like," Jo said with a smile.

43
00:03:53.095 --> 00:03:55.616
"Let's stop talking and fly these kites!"

44
00:03:56.028 --> 00:03:57.289
Nan said impatiently.

45
00:03:57.309 --> 00:04:00.952
"I don't know how to—" Daisy began.

46
00:04:00.972 --> 00:04:05.296
"Don't worry, we'll show you what to do," Tommy said.

47
00:04:07.298 --> 00:04:13.022
He rushed to help Nan while Nat, with some effort, persuaded Bess to release her little kite.

48
00:04:14.443 --> 00:04:17.206
Demi was concerned that Jo would feel neglected.

49
00:04:17.226 --> 00:04:20.729
"Let's help Aunt Jo first," he said.

50
00:04:20.749 --> 00:04:27.174
"Hold onto the string, Aunt Jo, and one of us will toss the kite in the air."

51
00:04:27.194 --> 00:04:32.137
"You're very considerate, Demi, but here's a boy who'll help me."

52
00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:37.321
Jo smiled as her husband peeped over the rock.

53
00:04:38.542 --> 00:04:42.685
The professor came out at once and tossed Jo's kite into the air.

54
00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:51.491
She ran off with it, while the children enjoyed the sight of their favorite adult behaving like one

55
00:04:51.511 --> 00:04:51.892
of them.

56
00:04:54.160 --> 00:05:00.223
Eventually all the kites soared into the air, where they floated like colorful birds.

57
00:05:01.863 --> 00:05:07.746
Nan raced far across the field, but Bess allowed her kite to go only on short flights.

58
00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:15.209
"Beautiful kite," Bess said, admiring the pictures Tommy had painted on it.

59
00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:21.692
Jo delighted in her giant kite, which seemed as adventurous as its owner.

60
00:05:23.316 --> 00:05:29.422
The kite caught on trees, almost fell into the river, and finally flew so high that it was

61
00:05:29.482 --> 00:05:30.964
a mere speck in the sky.

62
00:05:33.306 --> 00:05:38.411
After a while everyone grew tired and fastened the kite strings to a fence.

63
00:05:38.431 --> 00:05:43.015
"Did you ever have such a wonderful time?"

64
00:05:43.436 --> 00:05:46.959
Nat asked, lying on the ground and watching the kites fly.

65
00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:53.323
"Not since I last flew a kite years ago when I was a girl," Jo said.

66
00:05:53.343 --> 00:05:59.607
"I wish I had known you then because you must have been so much fun," Tommy said.

67
00:06:01.528 --> 00:06:04.790
Jo laughed and pulled Teddy and Rob onto her lap.

68
00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:11.373
"I might have been fun, but I'm sorry to say I was also a naughty little girl."

69
00:06:11.393 --> 00:06:15.476
"Tell us about the last time you flew a kite," Nat said.

70
00:06:16.648 --> 00:06:22.390
"Uncle Laurie and I were having a grand time flying kites when suddenly we heard voices.

71
00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:28.712
Some people were returning from a picnic, and I was embarrassed to be seen flying a kite at

72
00:06:28.752 --> 00:06:29.252
my age.

73
00:06:30.552 --> 00:06:36.994
I was 15, and I knew everyone would laugh at me because my wild ways always amused the

74
00:06:37.034 --> 00:06:40.215
neighbors." "You sound just like Nan!"

75
00:06:40.455 --> 00:06:43.416
Tommy said, which earned him a swat from Nan.

76
00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:46.965
"So what happened next?"

77
00:06:47.285 --> 00:06:48.026
Demi asked.

78
00:06:48.046 --> 00:06:53.450
"Uncle Laurie took out his pocketknife and cut our kite strings.

79
00:06:54.670 --> 00:07:00.694
Away flew the kites, and when the picnickers arrived, we were picking flowers like proper young people.

80
00:07:02.195 --> 00:07:06.678
After that, I decided to wait until I was an adult before I flew a kite again."

81
00:07:06.699 --> 00:07:10.261
"Then it's a good thing we made one for you!"

82
00:07:10.541 --> 00:07:11.982
Tommy said with delight.

83
00:07:13.163 --> 00:07:17.369
Jo nodded in agreement and went over to get her kite from the fence.

84
00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:21.870
"It's almost time for supper."

85
00:07:24.151 --> 00:07:25.991
"Wasn't our party wonderful?"

86
00:07:26.291 --> 00:07:27.912
Nat asked Jo and the girls.

87
00:07:27.932 --> 00:07:32.513
"Yes!" the females all cried together.

88
00:07:32.533 --> 00:07:35.234
"And do you know why that was?"

89
00:07:35.694 --> 00:07:36.435
Jo asked.

90
00:07:38.015 --> 00:07:41.036
"Because all your guests behaved themselves!"
